# agentcore/.env.local.example — AC-4 scaffold.
# Copy to agentcore/.env.local (gitignored via the repo-wide `.env.*` rule)
# and fill in. NO secrets are ever committed.
#
# The agent service reads exactly these variables:
#   src/agent-service/server.ts  -> WD_AGENT_PORT, WD_AGENT_DATA_DIR,
#                                   WD_AGENT_CLAIM_DB, WD_MACHINE_TOKEN_HASH
#   src/provider.ts              -> WD_PROVIDER, WD_BASE_URL, WD_MODEL,
#                                   WD_API_KEY (openai-compatible path);
#                                   WD_BEDROCK_MODEL, WD_AWS_REGION (bedrock)
#
# Deploy note (AC-5): non-secret operational vars are pinned in
# agentcore.json envVars. Secrets (WD_API_KEY, WD_MACHINE_TOKEN_HASH) must
# reach the runtime through a secrets mechanism Joe approves at deploy
# (AgentCore Identity / deploy-time env injection) — never in git.

# --- Model provider (RULING M4: bedrock is the documented default) ---
# agentcore.json pins WD_PROVIDER=bedrock for the deployed runtime;
# the openai-compatible shape below is the offline/CI escape hatch
# (provider.ts required()s these three when WD_PROVIDER=openai-compatible).
# WD_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
# WD_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# WD_MODEL=gpt-4o
# WD_API_KEY=sk-...

# Bedrock default path: credentials come from the AWS default chain via the
# runtime execution role; region/model have code defaults
# (global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6, us-east-1) — override here if needed.
# WD_BEDROCK_MODEL=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
# WD_AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# --- Agent service runtime shape ---
# Must match the AgentCore HTTP contract (port 8080) — do not change for
# AgentCore deploys. Local default is already 8080.
# WD_AGENT_PORT=8080

# Persistent session mount. The runtime mounts sessionStorage at /mnt/data
# (agentcore.json); run state lives in the agent subdirectory beneath it.
# Durable decisions still live in OUR store via the decision API — this
# mount is same-session resume only (spike-log Day 7).
# WD_AGENT_DATA_DIR=/mnt/data/agent

# Claim DB defaults INSIDE the data directory (server.ts): only set if you
# need to relocate it.
# WD_AGENT_CLAIM_DB=/mnt/data/agent/consumption.db

# --- Machine-principal auth (AC-2) ---
# sha256 hex of the scoped service token. Absent = the service refuses all
# invocations (fail closed). The runtime verifies the credential delivered
# INSIDE each invocation payload (body.credential), not an Authorization
# header — the platform boundary authenticates via SigV4/OAuth.
# Generate: printf '%s' "$TOKEN" | shasum -a 256
# WD_MACHINE_TOKEN_HASH=<64-hex sha256 of the service token>
